# Ownership here is a gate, not a notification list: the "Change Class Review
# Gate" ruleset turns every pattern below into a required code-owner approval
# that no OrganizationAdmin bypass clears. Deliberately no catch-all — an
# unowned path needs only the Baseline approval, which is what makes the gate
# class-based instead of blanket, and what keeps the set of changes that can
# deadlock small enough for the reviewers this org actually has.
#
# Two owners on every line so that whoever authors a change, someone who did
# not author it can still approve it. A GitHub App cannot appear here, so the
# agent identity can satisfy the Baseline count but never a code-owner gate.
#
# Last matching pattern wins. Class definitions and the incident evidence
# behind each one: docs/adr/0024-review-gates-by-change-class.md

# Gate integrity and supply chain. Workflows here mint GitHub App tokens, one
# of them scoped across all four repos; tools/ holds the scripts CI trusts to
# fail; and this directory defines the gates themselves, which ungated can
# quietly narrow or delete themselves.
/.github/ @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root
/tools/ @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root
/renovate.json @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root

# Argo CD applies everything else in this repo, and root-app.yaml is the apex
# of that tree — a bad change here breaks the mechanism that would deploy its
# own fix.
/bootstrap/ @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root

# Platform-tenant services are the cluster's own control plane, secret
# material, and stateful storage. Owned wholesale rather than per service so a
# service added later is gated by default instead of silently ungated.
/tenants/platform/ @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root

# Tenant envelope templates and the per-tenant switches that select them fan a
# single edit out across every tenant namespace at once, including the
# NetworkPolicy isolation those namespaces depend on.
/helm-charts/tenant-envelope/ @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root
/tenants/*/tenant.yaml @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root

# platformctl is the interface agents drive the platform through; its lint and
# test gates have been silently inert before.
/cli/ @jdwillmsen @jdwlabs-root
